    "field": "Emission accounting",
    "problem": "The absence of official up-to-date CO2 emission inventories for China, and the inconsistency, lack of detail, and non-transparency of existing global datasets, hinder effective evidence-based climate policymaking for the world's largest emitter.",
    "method": "This study proposes a uniform accounting framework based on IPCC guidelines to construct detailed CO2 emission and energy inventories for China and its 30 provinces for 2016-2017, providing up-to-date and transparent data to supplement official estimates.",
    "task": "The task is to construct up-to-date carbon dioxide emission and energy inventories for China and its 30 provinces for the years 2016 and 2017, detailed by 47 economic sectors and various fossil fuel types.",
